// Gimmick catalogue, booking-game-design.md §3.4.
//
// A `Gimmick` is a `GimmickSeed` (id/name/category/alignmentLean/concept/
// promoLines, plus an optional prop) run through `deriveGimmickDefaults`,
// which fills in the mechanical numbers and a default look off the
// category when a seed doesn't specify its own — see
// engine/generate/gimmickDefaults.ts. Adding a new gimmick means adding one
// more seed to GIMMICK_SEEDS below; nothing else in this file changes.
//
// The first 28 (category 'Classic') are the original starter set and keep
// their original hand-set numbers and looks explicitly, so nothing about
// them moved when this file grew. Everything after that came out of a
// content pass drafted in docs/gimmicks-catalog-draft.md, for the
// signing-meeting module — see that file for the full character list,
// including tag-team and faction identities (data/groupGimmicks.ts) and a
// few entries deliberately cut for sitting too close to real wrestling IP.
//
// territoryFit is left empty everywhere — territories don't exist until M6
// data lands; generation treats a missing entry as neutral (0) affinity.

